    "body": "> _\"since all angles in canvas is related to the x-axis, rotate the conic gradient by 90 degrees such that the gradient starts from x-axis.\"_ I have no idea what this means\r\n\r\nThis means other angles in the canvas API start from the X axis. See `context.arc()` and `context.ellipse()`, and `context.rotate()`: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#building-paths\r\n\r\nPersonally I think it is better to be consistent between canvas methods, than between CSS and canvas for this single method and then inconsistent for the others. /cc @whatwg/canvas\r\n\r\nSee also https://mobile.twitter.com/domenic/status/1391845024497799170",
